{"title":"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem C","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the three-digit positive integers of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb6b0d20bc894e3e628e58c19b0a1a537d5e175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are digits with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79c96e270e148516fb5dd4a73725d8be87c80c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />. How many of these integers are divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_for_11_proof\" title=\"Divisibility rules/Rule for 11 proof\">divisibility rule for 11</a>, we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6f0005a1e396cc9c03bf3f86993eba6b1af477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - y + 0 = x - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"17\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are digits and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff0c7fac58b2b7bb0901fedc86ff4757284388be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 &gt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e33fa7c7b2ce1a18e6e0a6d3ef6c08bd1958722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. This means that our number is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/061a38ca5ef42c5ed1b0364f877215ba2cb11385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{xx0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem B\">seat B</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7b75ce988b8a358682c0e6f8b4c78a9c5ac02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 20$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/061a38ca5ef42c5ed1b0364f877215ba2cb11385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{xx0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, we already see that all possible numbers are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the number always has a ones digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the last two digits must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> due to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_for_11_proof\" title=\"Divisibility rules/Rule for 11 proof\">divisibility rule for 4</a>.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea768618848c1aea8a32490c327911e8ab7243a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7da1b75cc1a945018db7316c26d618ca11ff9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/62434ae80ca145c20f0fbc7563f5151371ed163c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" /> values.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem B\">seat B</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7b75ce988b8a358682c0e6f8b4c78a9c5ac02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 20$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, and the number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that the number must also be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d878a1b6cea5cc592805e35253c73903df8735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\times 11 = 220$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> do not share any common factors except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/e/a9e622e054ba95d99f26093ba5434ec85431e026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{880}{220} = \\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" /> three-digit numbers divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6f941fab390e81243e1cd2b40c6178f03ab3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$220$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC\">2017 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<b